This Express handler receives a batch of scans from the Flutter app when a handheld reconnects (usually 50 to 400 scans) and stores them. Duplicates are expected because the app resends until it gets a 200, so I rely on a unique key on device and sequence number. I am unsure about the loop doing one insert per scan, and about what happens if one row is bad halfway through. Core of it:

for (const s of req.body.scans) {
  await db.query('INSERT INTO scans (device_id, seq, code) VALUES ($1,$2,$3) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING', [s.device, s.seq, s.code]);
}

Product listing for a Vue storefront on Postgres. The slow query is page 100 of a category with OFFSET, about 1.8 seconds on 180 thousand products. I rewrote it as keyset pagination, but I am not sure the index fits it, or what to do when two products share a created_at:

SELECT id, name, price FROM products WHERE category_id = $1 AND (created_at, id) < ($2, $3) ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC LIMIT 24;

The index is (category_id, created_at, id). Please check the row comparison and the index.
